## Claim
Text: "The iPhone 12 won’t come with earphones and a charging adapter."
Claim date: October 14, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Apple officially announce the iPhone 12 smartphone in October 2020?
Answer: Yes, Apple officially announced the iPhone 12 in October 2020. According to the press release, "Apple® today unveiled iPhone® 12 and iPhone 12 mini with 5G technology" on October 13, 2020.

Source URL: https://www.samoaobserver.ws/category/article/72577

### According to Apple's official product page and press release for the iPhone 12, what items were listed as being included inside the retail box?
Answer: According to the search result, which cites Apple's official statement, the iPhone 12 retail box included only the phone itself and a USB-C to Lightning cable. Apple explicitly stated: "As part of our efforts to reach our environmental goals, iPhone 12 and iPhone 12 mini do not include a power adapter or EarPods. Please use your current Apple power adapter and headphones, or purchase these accessories separately."

Source URL: https://wccftech.com/apple-iphone-12-mini-and-iphone-12-pro-max-retail-box-contents/

### Did Apple state that the iPhone 12 retail box would not include a pair of wired EarPods/earphones?
Answer: The search result does not contain an official statement from Apple confirming that the iPhone 12 box would not include wired EarPods. Instead, it reports predictions from analyst Ming-Chi Kuo, stating: "Apple may not include a power adapter and earphones in the box with the new iPhone 12... according to a respected leaker." The article is based on leaks and analyst speculation rather than an official Apple announcement.

Source URL: https://www.dailymail.co.uk/sciencetech/article-8470069/Leaker-says-new-iPhones-wont-include-EarPods-power-adaptor.html

### Did Apple state that the iPhone 12 retail box would not include a USB power adapter/charging brick?
Answer: The search result does not contain any direct statement from Apple about the iPhone 12's retail box not including a USB power adapter/charging brick. The information presented is based on rumors and analyst predictions (specifically from analyst Ming-Chi Kuo) rather than an official announcement from Apple.

Source URL: https://news.wirefly.com/2020/06/28/iphone-12-no-charger-box

### Was the absence of earphones and a charging adapter in the iPhone 12 box a policy change that Apple explicitly announced to the public?
Answer: Yes, Apple explicitly announced this policy change to the public during its iPhone 12 launch event on October 13, 2020. As the article states, "the biggest surprise of the day was Apple announcing this year's devices will not include the traditional charger and EarPods," and Lisa Jackson, Apple's VP of environment, policy and social initiatives, explicitly stated during the event: "We're removing these items from the iPhone box, which reduces carbon emissions and avoids the mining and use of precious materials."

Source URL: https://www.dailymail.co.uk/sciencetech/article-8840611/Apple-customers-outraged-learning-799-iPhone-12-NOT-include-charger-EarPods.html

### What reason did Apple officially give for omitting the earphones and the charging adapter from the iPhone 12 packaging?
Answer: Apple officially cited environmental and waste reduction reasons for omitting the earphones and charging adapter. Lisa Jackson, Apple's VP of environment, policy and social initiatives, stated: "We know that customers have been accumulating USB power adapters, and that producing millions of unneeded adapters consumes resources and adds to our carbon footprint." She also noted that Apple believes there are "over 700 million pairs of wired EarPods and around 2 billion power adapters in circulation around the world." Additionally, Apple mentioned that the smaller box would allow them to "fit 70% more iPhones onto a shipping pallet."

Source URL: https://www.cnbc.com/2020/10/14/apple-praised-for-removing-earpods-and-charger-from-iphone-12-box.html

### Did the omission of earphones and a charging adapter apply to all iPhone 12 models sold by Apple, including the iPhone 12 mini, iPhone 12, iPhone 12 Pro, and iPhone 12 Pro Max?
Answer: Yes, the omission of earphones (EarPods) and a charging adapter (power adapter) applied to the entire iPhone 12 lineup. According to the source, "the entire iPhone 12 lineup ships without EarPods or a power adapter in the box," with Apple's website explicitly stating that "iPhone 12 and iPhone 12 mini do not include a power adapter or EarPods," and "a similar message shown for the iPhone 12 Pro and iPhone 12 Pro Max."

Source URL: https://www.macrumors.com/2020/10/13/iphone-12-ships-without-earpods-or-charger/

### What accessory, if any, did Apple include in the iPhone 12 box to allow the phone to be connected to power or other devices?
Answer: According to the source, the iPhone 12 box includes only "the phone itself and a USB-C to Lightning cable." Apple removed both the power adapter and EarPods from the retail box as part of its environmental efforts, so the only included accessory for connecting to power or other devices is the USB-C to Lightning cable—meaning users need a compatible USB-C charger to actually power the device.

Source URL: https://wccftech.com/apple-iphone-12-mini-and-iphone-12-pro-max-retail-box-contents/

### Did the immediately preceding iPhone model, the iPhone 11, ship with both earphones and a charging adapter in its retail box?
Answer: Yes. According to the search result, the iPhone 11 originally did ship with both earphones and a charging adapter, as the article notes that "Even if they came in the box before" when discussing how Apple no longer bundles these accessories with any handset. The removal of these accessories applied to the iPhone 12 launch in October 2020 (the claim's date), but the iPhone 11's original retail box—released in September 2019—included both EarPods and a USB power adapter.

Source URL: https://www.cultofmac.com/725512/apple-charger-headphones-with-iphone-12-11-se/

### Were independent teardowns or unboxing reports of the iPhone 12 (published on or after October 14, 2020) consistent with the claim that neither earphones nor a charging adapter were included in the box?
Answer: Yes, the search result confirms that reports of the iPhone 12's retail box contents were consistent with the claim. The article explicitly states that "they don't ship with EarPods or the charger in the box" and that the phones ship with "the bare minimum - just the phone itself and a USB-C to Lightning cable." It also quotes Apple's official statement: "As part of our efforts to reach our environmental goals, iPhone 12 and iPhone 12 mini do not include a power adapter or EarPods."

